<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Stacks evaluation report</title>
  <style>
    body { margin: 0; background: #fbf7ef; color: #302d29; font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
    main { max-width: 1100px; margin: auto; padding: 48px 24px; }
    h1, h2 { font-family: Georgia, serif; }
    h1 { font-size: 3rem; }
    a { color: #7b3042; }
    .notice { border-left: 4px solid #7b3042; padding: 12px 18px; background: #f0e7d9; }
    .table { overflow-x: auto; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .92rem; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d5cbbb; }
    th { background: #f0e7d9; }
    code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  </style>
</head>
<body><main>
  <p>STACKS / MEASUREMENT</p>
  <h1>What the evidence supports.</h1>
  <p class="notice">{{ e.statement }}</p>
  <p>Backend: <strong>{{ e.dataset.backend }}</strong>. Generated {{ e.generated_at }}.</p>
  <p>{{ e.dataset.catalog_size | number(0) }} books and {{ e.dataset.evaluated_users | number(0) }} readers;
    {{ e.protocol.name }}. The source supplies no rating timestamps, so row ordering is a proxy.</p>
  <h2>Model comparison</h2>
  <div class="table"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>NDCG with interval</th><th>Retrieval recall with interval</th><th>Observed coverage and resampling range</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{% for row in e.metrics %}<tr><td>{{ row.label }}</td><td>{{ row.ndcg | estimate }}</td><td>{{ row.recall200 | estimate }}</td><td>{{ row.coverage | estimate }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Observed leader: <strong>{{ e.winner.observed }}</strong>.
    Corrected selection: <strong>{{ e.winner.corrected if e.winner.corrected else "not established" }}</strong>.</p>
  <h2>Off-policy evidence</h2>
  <ul>{% for name in ["simulator", "crosscheck", "open_bandit", "demo_logs"] %}
    <li><strong>{{ name }}: {{ e.ope[name].status }}</strong>. {{ e.ope[name].get("detail", "See the complete results for measured estimates.") }}</li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>
  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>{% for limitation in e.limitations %}<li>{{ limitation }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  <p>The public frontend uses GitHub Pages. The local Python API is independently runnable.</p>
  {% if hosting.get("verified_for_publication") %}
  <p>The <a href="{{ hosting.url }}/health">live Worker/D1 API</a> passed public checks
    and an independent database read. The free host buffers long streams, so updates
    use bounded SSE connections with EventSource reconnection and Last-Event-ID replay.</p>
  {% else %}<p>Public API verification is pending.</p>{% endif %}
  {% if latency %}
  <p>Measured request latency: p50 {{ latency.p50 | estimate(2) }} ms;
    p99 {{ latency.p99 | estimate(2) }} ms. {{ latency.requests }} requests,
    concurrency {{ latency.concurrency }}. This small sequential sample is not a capacity or SLO claim.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p><a href="https://mekala27-45.github.io/stacks/">Open the bookstore</a> ·
    <a href="https://github.com/mekala27-45/stacks/blob/main/RESULTS.md">Complete results and protocol diagnostics</a></p>
</main></body>
</html>
